<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Pilot study principles">
  <div><strong>Feasibility first</strong><span>A pilot asks whether a future study can be done, should be done and how it should be designed, not whether a small sample has proven efficacy.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Progression criteria</strong><span>Recruitment, completion, sample quality, adherence, tolerance and protocol deviations should determine whether and how a project advances.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Status stays visible</strong><span>Concept, protocol development, approved, recruiting, completed and analyzed are different stages and should never be collapsed into “study underway.”</span></div>
</div>

